<SddInterviewProtocol keywords="interview, coverage-map, triage, amplification, rounds, defaults-first, weak-spots, closure, stakes-split, one-question-per-message, ask-tool-binding, sdd-interview-protocol" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Run ONE operator interview for an authoring step. Loaded lazily by a branch step (scope
    STEP_2 / STEP_3, infra STEP_2, interface STEP_2, module STEP_2) via `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE`; the calling
    step supplies the scope-type + its focus and stays the owner of what gets written. Inherits
    the router core (language, dialogue, safeguard, diverge, no-narration) — not repeated here.

    This protocol equips the interview declared by `AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD` with instruments: a
    live coverage map, an amplification triage, defaults-first rounds, and a map-based closure
    criterion. The safeguard axiom stays the source of the interviewing instinct; this directive
    only gives it structure.

    Input — scope-type, calling-step focus, intake gathered so far. Output — a closed coverage
    map + the captured answers and decisions, returned to the calling step. This directive writes
    no artifact; control returns to the caller at CLOSE.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE, AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION">
    {{> "axiom/interview/ax-coverage-map-closure"}}

    {{> "axiom/interview/ax-defaults-first"}}

    {{> "axiom/interview/ax-amplification-opt-in"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_STAKES_SPLIT">
      The stakes of a question decide its delivery form — this overrides any round-grouping default:
      - A **развилка** (architecture, a trust boundary, an irreversible or hard-to-undo choice) → ONE
        question per message, full form per `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT`, answered via `AskUserQuestion`
        before the next question is composed.
      - A **default confirmation** (naming, a low-risk default, an obvious yes/no) → batched, up to 4
        per `AskUserQuestion` call, per `BATCH_CONFIRM_FORMAT`.
      Unsure which it is → treat as развилка. Burying a genuine fork inside a batch is the exact
      failure this axiom exists to prevent.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL">
      Развилки go strictly one at a time: compose question N+1 only after the answer to question N is
      in. Each next question MUST account for every prior answer in the interview — a question whose
      premise an earlier answer already invalidated is a protocol defect, not a style issue. The
      counter in `## Вопрос <X> из <Y>` is owned here: X is this question's ordinal in the interview;
      Y is questions already asked plus развилки still open on the coverage map. When thread-pulling
      opens a new topic, Y grows and the growth shows in the next map line — never silently.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_ASK_TOOL_BINDING">
      Every развилка ends in one `AskUserQuestion` call, bound to its chat message:
      - The chat message carries the full material (`QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT`); the ASK call carries
        only short option labels + one-line descriptions — never move the argument itself into the ASK.
      - Options appear in the ASK in the SAME order they were printed in the message.
      - A recommendation prints first in the message too (letter A) and carries «(рекомендую)» in its
        ASK label — printed order and recommended-first then agree.
      - «Other» is supplied by the tool automatically; never add a manual equivalent.
      - Tool unavailable → drop only the ASK call; the развилка message still follows
        `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT` and the answer arrives as free text, otherwise falling back to the
        caller's plain-text `QUESTION_FORMAT` when one applies. Batched default confirmations use one
        ASK call covering 2–4 questions.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_VISUAL_WHEN_RELATIONAL">
      When a question's subject is relational — a flow, a boundary, a structure, a lifecycle, or
      variants that differ in shape — draw a compact ASCII picture BEFORE the variants, per
      `formats/diagram-vocabulary.xml` (`AX_DIAGRAM_DISCIPLINE`: ≤7 nodes, one diagram per idea). A
      question about a single scalar choice stays prose; a diagram of one node is noise, not clarity.
      The same relation later lands in the spec as mermaid — the module/scope Overview if it is the
      floor diagram (`AX_OVERVIEW_DIAGRAM_FLOOR`), else inline where the section needs it. The chat
      ASCII is the operator's preview of the shape they are approving.
    </Axiom>

    <Axiom id="AX_SCANNABLE_TEXT">
      The operator surfs a question message, they do not wade through it: bold marks the load-bearing
      word inside a bullet, not the whole sentence; each block opens with its own emoji anchor;
      paragraphs stay ≤3 lines; no monolithic prose wall. Emotion is seasoning, not paint — anchors and
      an occasional marker, never an emoji on every line.
    </Axiom>
  </BeliefState>

  <TopicCatalog>
    Base topics — every interview starts with these (map labels in Russian):

    | Topic | Substance |
    |---|---|
    | Цель и не-цель | what this scope delivers; what it explicitly refuses to do in this iteration |
    | Потребители | who consumes the result and what they expect from it |
    | Слабые места | MANDATORY: holes, contradictions, unstated expectations of the intake — name them to the operator, per `AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD` |
    | Внешние зависимости | what outside this scope must exist / hold for the design to stand |

    scope-type block — append per the caller's scope-type:

    | scope-type | Topics |
    |---|---|
    | product | Пользователи (who exactly, how many) · Метрика успеха/провала (both, not only success) · Зачем сейчас (why this, why now) · Worst case (the worst plausible scenario and who pays for it) |
    | library | Разработчики-потребители (which teams / repos) · DX (how consumption should feel; feeds Golden DX) · Версии (versioning + compatibility promises) |
    | infrastructure | Окружения (dev / CI / prod parity) · Доставка (how changes reach consumers) |
    | interface | Стороны контракта (producers and consumers, who owns the schema) · Эволюция (how the contract changes without breaking consumers) |

    The calling step MAY narrow or extend the block for its focus (e.g. scope STEP_3 keeps only
    what the Requirements Gate still misses); «Слабые места» stays on every map.
  </TopicCatalog>

  <AmplificationCatalog>
    Deep-dive modules; each is a separate directive authored elsewhere and loaded lazily
    (`AX_AMPLIFICATION_OPT_IN`):

    | Amplification | Directive | Triage trigger |
    |---|---|---|
    | security | `ai/directives/sdd-v2/amplify-security.directive.xml` | external users, or data crossing a trust boundary |
    | nfr | `ai/directives/sdd-v2/amplify-nfr.directive.xml` | load / latency / volume significant enough to shape the design |
    | storage | `ai/directives/sdd-v2/amplify-storage.directive.xml` | state persisted beyond a single run |
    | observability | `ai/directives/sdd-v2/amplify-observability.directive.xml` | someone must diagnose this in production |
  </AmplificationCatalog>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_HIGH_STAKES_SKIP` | Operator insists on skipping an unclosed high-stakes topic — name the concrete cost (per `AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD`); on a confirmed skip record `[✗ skip: <причина>]` in the map and proceed |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_INIT_MAP">
      <Goal>Build and show the coverage map.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Assemble the map: base topics + the scope-type block from `TopicCatalog`, narrowed /
        extended by the calling step's focus. Mark topics the intake already answers `[✔]` — ask
        only what a decision still needs. Render per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT` with a one-line plan
        («что осталось закрыть»); proceed straight to triage.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_TRIAGE">
      <Goal>Decide which amplifications this task deserves.</Goal>
      <Action>
        One compact block of 3–5 closed questions (yes / no / short pick), mandatory even when the
        task looks small: external users or external data? load significant? state persisted?
        must this be diagnosable in production? — plus at most one triage question specific to the
        intake. From the answers, propose an amplification set per `AmplificationCatalog` with the
        small-task default «none active» (`AX_AMPLIFICATION_OPT_IN`); operator confirms. Confirmed
        amplifications become map topics on the «Усиления» line. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_ROUNDS">
      <Goal>Close the map, one topic at a time, in the shape its stakes demand.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Loop until the map is closed (`AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`); each round:
        1. Show the map per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT`, pick the next open topic, mark it `[▶]`.
        2. Split by stakes (`AX_STAKES_SPLIT`): a развилка → one message per
           `QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT`, answered before the next question is composed
           (`AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL`); a default confirmation → collect it and batch up to 4
           per `BATCH_CONFIRM_FORMAT`.
        3. Shape each question per `AX_DEFAULTS_FIRST` — a concrete default to confirm or correct —
           and bind its chat message to the `AskUserQuestion` call per `AX_ASK_TOOL_BINDING`.
        4. After each answer, update the map and pull the thread per `AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`
           (new hole → new / reopened topic; a развилка whose premise the answer invalidated is
           recomposed, not asked as planned — `AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL`).
        5. An amplification topic opens → `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE` its directive from
           `AmplificationCatalog` and run its questions as this round, split by stakes the same way.
        A skip request on a high-stakes topic → `H_HIGH_STAKES_SKIP`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_CLOSE">
      <Goal>Verify closure and return to the caller.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Gate per `AX_COVERAGE_MAP_CLOSURE`: every topic `[✔]` or `[✗ skip: <причина>]` — an open
        or `[▶]` topic sends the flow back to STEP_3. Show the final map + a compact digest of
        answers and decisions (Russian), including skips with reasons. Hand the digest to the
        calling step — it owns the Approval Check, artifact writing, and any Decision Log entries.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    The map per `COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT` opens every round — it is the operator's progress view, so
    keep it current and compact (per `AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`, the map replaces narration about
    what the interview is doing).

    {{> "contract/interview/coverage-map-format"}}

    <Contract id="QUESTION_MESSAGE_FORMAT">
      The развилка message — one question, full context, live markdown (never fenced). Blocks in
      order; skip a block only when genuinely empty:

      1. Coverage map line (`COVERAGE_MAP_FORMAT`).
      2. `## Вопрос <X> из <Y> · <topic, no question mark>` — X/Y per `AX_ONE_QUESTION_SEQUENTIAL`.
      3. `**Решаем одной строкой:** <the fork, one sentence>`.
      4. An ASCII diagram — only when the subject is relational (`AX_VISUAL_WHEN_RELATIONAL`).
      5. `**📌 Что известно**` — 2–5 bullets, load-bearing words bold, specific to THIS question —
         not a restate of the session (`AX_SCANNABLE_TEXT`).
      6. `**⚖️ Варианты**` — each variant: `**<Letter>. <name>**` then `✅ <pros, · -separated>` /
         `⚠️ <cons, · -separated>`. 3+ variants with comparable criteria → a criteria×variant table
         INSTEAD of the lists (rows = criteria, columns = variants; the killer cell bold).
      7. `**🎯 Куда клонюсь:** <letter> — <why, one sentence>` — omit on high-stakes questions where
         pre-anchoring is wrong (`AX_DEFAULTS_FIRST`).
      8. The `AskUserQuestion` call (`AX_ASK_TOOL_BINDING`) — options in printed order.

      <Example>
        Покрытие: Цель/не-цель [✔] · Потребители [✔] · **формат спеки [▶]** · Зависимости [ ] · Слабые места [ ]

        ## Вопрос 3 из 6 · Куда переезжает разросшаяся ячейка Entity Inventory

        **Решаем одной строкой:** ячейка таблицы с абзацем на восемь предложений не читается во
        вьювере — куда девать текст при миграции на v2-формат.

        ```
        [ячейка: 8 предложений] ──migrate──► ??? ──рендер во вьювере──► [читаемая таблица]
                                              │
                                     куда: подсекция? свернуть? урезать?
        ```

        **📌 Что известно**
        - Правило F2 запрещает **абзацы и списки внутри ячейки** — только одна короткая строка.
        - Развёрнутый текст должен **переехать в подсекцию под таблицей**, а не исчезнуть.
        - `sdd-check` уже умеет **считать длину ячейки** — порог просто пока не задан.

        **⚖️ Варианты**

        **A. Короткая ячейка + подсекция `### <ID> — детали`**
        ✅ таблица остаётся индексом · ничего не теряется · механически проверяемо
        ⚠️ спека становится длиннее на число подсекций

        **B. Урезать ячейку до одной фразы, остальное — в Decision Log**
        ✅ таблица короче любой подсекции
        ⚠️ решение теряет прямую связь со строкой таблицы — придётся искать отдельно

        **🎯 Куда клонюсь:** A — подсекция держит связь «строка → детали», ничего не отрывается от
        таблицы.

        (AskUserQuestion: «A. Подсекция под таблицей (рекомендую)» · «B. В Decision Log»)
      </Example>
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="BATCH_CONFIRM_FORMAT">
      Default confirmations — one compact block, then ONE `AskUserQuestion` call with 2–4 questions.
      Per item: one bold line (the default) + one plain line (the alternative and when it wins). No
      «Что известно» blocks, no diagrams. An item that provokes discussion is promoted to a развилка
      in the next message, not resolved inside the batch.
    </Contract>

    <Contract id="NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT">
      Rendered by the CALLING step's final step, after its artifact is written and verified. Shape:

      1. One ✅ line — what was produced and what was checked
         (`✅ Спека <path> записана · язык проверен · <N> диаграмм`).
      2. `**Что дальше?**` + one `AskUserQuestion` call. Options (2–4) come from the caller's own
         candidate table; the recommended option first with «(рекомендую)»; CHAINED options are
         first-class («декомпозиция + критик следом», «scaffold + сразу execute») — one pick launches
         the whole chain, the agent runs it without stopping between links unless a link fails.
         Always include «Закончить сессию» last.
      3. On pick: invoke the corresponding skill(s) / directive flow(s) directly — never answer with
         «запусти /sdd-X сам».
    </Contract>
  </ChatOutput>
</SddInterviewProtocol>
